statement:
In the backward kernel for unfold, the core loop looks roughly like:
```cpp
for (int i = 0; i < unfolded_len; ++i) {
    atomicAdd(&grad_input[idx(i)], grad_output[i] * weight[i]);
}
```
The repeated atomicAdd across the unfolded_len dimension creates a serialization bottleneck, which is why the backward pass is much slower.
